        {
            "+content": "Rejected as an apprentice by the celebrated Kano Eitoku, painter Hasegawa Tohaku struggles to establish himself in Kyoto. When he risks his life to see Eitoku's masterpieces inside a burning castle, his ambition is rekindled. Against the upheaval of sixteenth-century Japan, Tohaku fights for recognition while confronting the losses that will shape his art. Chie Shimomoto's complete, one-volume historical drama imagines the turbulent life of one of Japan's great painters.",
